From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:54:15 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: two-finger swipe back and forward on web
 pages

Issue #21. A horizontal two-finger swipe on a page did nothing. Chrome's
history swiper (the edge arrow that follows the fingers, then navigates)
lives in the render widget view's event delegate, which Chrome's
WebContentsViewDelegate creates; Open Arc returned no view delegate
(patch 0012) so that the shell could draw the page's menus.

The embedder now returns its own OpenArcWebContentsViewDelegate. It
gives each page's render widget view Chrome's
ChromeRenderWidgetHostViewMacDelegate (none for popups), which navigates
with chrome::GoBack / GoForward on the WebContents and needs no Chrome
window. Everything else keeps content's defaults: the context menu is
still drawn by the shell from the tab's WebContentsDelegate
(HandleContextMenu runs before the view delegate is asked), drops pass
through unchanged, and focus handling is content's own.
